---
// Homepage — ticket 7 (Build the Homepage), Map — neuron.github.io Site (2.5.0).
// Folds ticket 4's winning prototype direction (Minimal Text-First, branch
// prototype/ticket4-homepage-variants, commit e8b6bbd) into the real site,
// with ticket 2's settled copy and Map — SEO & GEO Groundwork's ticket 3
// JSON-LD convention (WebSite + SoftwareApplication + FAQPage, Person author).
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const canonicalUrl = 'https://kovartravis.github.io/neuron/';
const githubUrl = 'https://github.com/kovartravis/neuron';

const person = {
	'@type': 'Person',
	name: 'Travis Kovar',
	url: 'https://github.com/kovartravis',
};

const faqs = [
	{
		q: 'Does neuron send my code or memory to the cloud?',
		a: 'No. neuron runs 100% offline — it embeds text locally with ONNX models and stores everything in a local SQLite/markdown store. No API keys, no telemetry, nothing leaves your machine.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Does neuron work with Cursor and Codex, or only Claude Code?',
		a: 'neuron ships harness adapters for Claude Code, OpenAI Codex CLI, Cursor, and GitHub Copilot CLI. Claude Code and Codex CLI get memory injected automatically on every turn; Cursor and Copilot CLI get it once per session, since those harnesses only expose a session-start hook.',
	},
	{
		q: 'How is neuron different from a CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md file?',
		a: "A CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md file is static prose an agent rereads in full every prompt, whether it's relevant or not, and it only grows over time. neuron stores memory as structured, schema-enforced entries and surfaces only what's relevant to the current query, instead of dumping one file into every prompt.",
	},
	{
		q: 'Is neuron free to use?',
		a: 'Yes. neuron is MIT-licensed and installs via npm or a standalone curl/PowerShell binary, with no account or API key required.',
	},
];

const jsonLd = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@graph': [
		{
			'@type': 'WebSite',
			name: 'neuron',
			url: canonicalUrl,
		},
		{
			'@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
			name: 'neuron',
			applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication',
			operatingSystem: 'macOS, Linux, Windows',
			url: canonicalUrl,
			license: 'https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT',
			offers: {
				'@type': 'Offer',
				price: '0',
				priceCurrency: 'USD',
			},
			author: person,
		},
		{
			'@type': 'FAQPage',
			mainEntity: faqs.map(({ q, a }) => ({
				'@type': 'Question',
				name: q,
				acceptedAnswer: {
					'@type': 'Answer',
					text: a,
				},
			})),
		},
	],
};
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>neuron — the local-first memory engine for coding agents</title>
		<meta
			name="description"
			content="neuron gives Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex persistent memory — 100% local, relevance-gated, and it stops your agent from repeating the same mistake twice."
		/>
		<link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />
		<link rel="icon" href={`${base}/favicon.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
		<style>
			:root {
				--mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', monospace;
				--sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif;
				--bg: #f7f5f0;
				--fg: #16150f;
				--fg-muted: #4a4941;
				--fg-faint: #7a7869;
				--accent: #1a5f3f;
				--rule: #ded9cb;
				--code-bg: #ece9e1;
			}
			* { box-sizing: border-box; }
			body {
				margin: 0;
				font-family: var(--sans);
				background: var(--bg);
				color: var(--fg);
			}
			code { font-family: var(--mono); }
			a { color: inherit; }

			.hero { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 8rem 1.5rem 5rem; text-align: center; }
			.hero h1 { font-size: 2.9rem; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
			.hero .sub { font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 auto 2.25rem; max-width: 52ch; }
			.inline-code {
				display: block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.85rem;
				background: var(--code-bg); color: var(--fg); padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
				border-radius: 6px; margin: 0 auto 0.6rem; max-width: 460px; text-align: left;
			}
			.alt { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--fg-faint); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
			.ctas { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; justify-content: center; align-items: center; }
			.btn { text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.95rem; }
			.btn.primary { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; padding: 0.75rem 1.6rem; border-radius: 4px; }
			.btn.ghost { color: var(--fg); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fg); padding-bottom: 2px; }

			.pillars { max-width: 620px; margin: 0 auto 4rem; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
			.pillar { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; padding: 1.75rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
			.pillar:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
			.pillar .num { font-size: 1.6rem; color: #cfc9b8; font-weight: 300; min-width: 2.2ch; }
			.pillar h3 { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
			.pillar p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.55; }

			.prose { max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto 5rem; padding: 0 1.5rem; font-size: 0.98rem; color: #33321f; line-height: 1.75; text-align: center; }
			.prose em { color: var(--accent); font-style: normal; }
			.aside { text-align: center; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--fg-faint); font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 5rem; padding: 0 1.5rem; }

			.faq { max-width: 620px; margin: 0 auto 7rem; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
			.faq h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 0 0 2rem; text-align: center; }
			.faq-item { padding: 1.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
			.faq-item:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
			.faq-item h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; }
			.faq-item p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.6; }

			footer { text-align: center; font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--fg-faint); padding: 0 1.5rem 4rem; }
			footer a { text-decoration: underline; }

			@media (max-width: 640px) {
				.hero { padding: 4rem 1.25rem 3rem; }
				.hero h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; }
				.hero .sub { font-size: 1rem; }
				.inline-code { max-width: 100%; font-size: 0.78rem; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; }
				.ctas { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.9rem; width: 100%; }
				.btn.primary { width: 100%; text-align: center; }
				.pillar { gap: 1rem; padding: 1.4rem 0; }
				.pillar .num { font-size: 1.3rem; min-width: 1.8ch; }
				.prose { font-size: 0.92rem; padding: 0 1.25rem; }
				.aside { padding: 0 1.25rem; }
			}

			/* Desktop two-column reflow — Map — Homepage Desktop Layout's Ticket 1
			   (Prototype the Desktop Two-Column Layout), "Pillars Beside Hero"
			   variant. Everything below 960px (including the 641-959px range)
			   is untouched — same single-column layout as before. */
			@media (min-width: 960px) {
				.hero-wrap {
					max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2rem;
					display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr; column-gap: 3.5rem; align-items: center;
				}
				.hero { max-width: none; margin: 0; padding: 7rem 0; text-align: left; }
				.hero .sub { margin: 0 0 2.25rem; max-width: 46ch; }
				.ctas { justify-content: flex-start; }
				.inline-code { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
				.pillars {
					max-width: none; margin: 0; padding: 2rem 2rem;
					background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 12px;
					box-shadow: 0 30px 70px -35px rgba(22,21,15,0.25);
				}
				.pillar { padding: 1.25rem 0; }
				.pillar:first-child { border-top: none; padding-top: 0; }
				.pillar:last-child { border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: 0; }
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="hero-wrap">
			<div class="hero">
				<h1>The local-first memory engine for coding agents</h1>
				<p class="sub">
					Not another cloud memory API. Not another bloated rules file dumped into every prompt.
					neuron gives Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex persistent memory — 100% local, relevance-gated,
					and it stops your agent from repeating the same mistake twice.
				</p>
				<code class="inline-code">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kovartravis/neuron/main/install.sh | sh</code>
				<div class="alt">or <code>npm install -g @kovartravis/neuron</code></div>
				<div class="ctas">
					<a class="btn primary" href={`${base}/docs/quickstart/`}>Get started</a>
					<a class="btn ghost" href={githubUrl}>View on GitHub</a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="pillars">
				<div class="pillar">
					<div class="num">01</div>
					<div>
						<h3>Zero-Cloud Privacy</h3>
						<p>Local ONNX embeddings + SQLite. No API keys, no telemetry, nothing leaves your machine.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="pillar">
					<div class="num">02</div>
					<div>
						<h3>Zero-Amnesia Execution</h3>
						<p>Pre-command lookup checks memory before every shell command runs, so agents stop debugging the same failure twice.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="pillar">
					<div class="num">03</div>
					<div>
						<h3>Context Budget Diet</h3>
						<p>Relevance-gated recall injects only what's relevant — nothing dumped into every prompt.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<p class="aside">also works as a CI check — <code>neuron scan --check</code> catches architecture drift before it merges</p>

		<p class="prose">
			Every agent starts each session with amnesia — the same bug gets debugged twice, the same
			convention gets re-explained, and static rules files pile up until nobody trusts them.
			<em>neuron</em> is what a coding agent remembers between sessions, without sending a single
			byte of your code to the cloud.
		</p>

		<div class="faq">
			<h2>Questions</h2>
			{faqs.map(({ q, a }) => (
				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>{q}</h3>
					<p>{a}</p>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>

		<footer>
			<a href={`${base}/docs/`}>Docs</a> · <a href={githubUrl}>GitHub</a> · MIT © Travis Kovar
		</footer>
	</body>
</html>
